        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Julian Weill, Bertolt Brecht, John Gay, Elisabeth Hauptmann\n- Works: The Threepenny Opera, The Beggar's Opera\n- Places: Germany, Chicago\n- Topics: composition, theatrical adaptation, collaboration\n\nFacts:\n- Kurt Julian Weill was a German composer who was active from the 1920s in Germany and in his later years in Chicago.\n- Kurt Julian Weill collaborated with Bertolt Brecht on productions including The Threepenny Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera is a play with music by Bertolt Brecht.\n- The Threepenny Opera was adapted from John Gay's 18th-century English ballad opera The Beggar's Opera.\n- Elisabeth Hauptmann was involved in the adaptation of The Beggar's Opera into The Threepenny Opera.",
