        "original_id": "bbd9cb88-6d92-5c45-bd13-4d955d4d82c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Weill, Bertolt Brecht, Elisabeth Hauptmann, John Gay, François Villon, Rudyard Kipling\n- Works: The Threepenny Opera, Mack the Knife, The Beggar's Opera\n- Concepts: play with music, ballad opera\n\nFacts:\n- In the 18th century, John Gay wrote the English ballad opera The Beggar's Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera is a play with music by Bertolt Brecht and Elisabeth Hauptmann.\n- The Threepenny Opera was adapted from John Gay's The Beggar's Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera has music by Kurt Weill.\n- The Threepenny Opera includes insertion ballads by François Villon and Rudyard Kipling.\n- Kurt Weill developed productions with Bertolt Brecht, including his best-known work The Threepenny Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera included the ballad Mack the Knife.",
